[OC]|cffffcc00Merchant camp (new in Forever):|r just inside the zone line at 10,72, the Azeroth Commerce Authority caravan - Supply Officer [TAR256390 Marcy Baker] (9.7,70.9) takes filled Waylaid Crates (A Sealed Crate) for money and Merchant's Favor: 15s at 12-18, 20s at 22, 30s at 25 and 2g at 28 per the Wowhead Forever zone data (which crate pays which, and the Favor per crate, are unverified). A dropped Waylaid Crate becomes a category crate when you read its label, and those are tradeable: the Ironforge AH had them at 4-22s on 6 Nov (Apprentice Herbs 11s plus about 2s of Silverleaf to fill it, Ore 12s plus about 4s of Copper Ore, Textiles 17s plus 20 Light Leather), so a bought-and-filled crate costs about what the hand-in pays back and the Favor is nearly free. Fill Ingots with the 20 Copper Bars you carry, Textiles with Light Leather only after your skill-ups; buy the Belt (skill 60) and Gloves (75) patterns here first; [TAR256734 Daniel Stitchsong] (10,72.4) sells six |cff66ff66Totemic Leather|r patterns for 30 Favor each (price unverified; the patterns bind on pickup) - Belt (skill 60, req 12, +4 Str +3 Sta +4 spell), Gloves (75, req 15, +4 Str +3 Sta +5 spell), Boots (85, req 17, +5 Str +4 Sta +6 spell), Hood (100, req 20), Tunic (110, req 22), Leggings (125, req 25); each piece also needs Pristine Leather (2/2/3/4/6/8) and Sulfuric Acid (1/2/3/4/6/8; Alchemy 40: 2 Pyrite + 1 Empty Vial each) - both about 4s apiece on the Ironforge AH on 6 Nov, so buy them. He does NOT sell the three Pristine-free pieces: |cff66ff66Armor|r (skill 75, req 15, +7 Str +3 Sta +3 Int +6 spell: 16 Light Leather, 2 Cured Light Hide, 1 acid), |cff66ff66Pants|r (100, req 20, +9 Str +4 Sta +4 Int +7 spell: 8 Medium Leather, 4 Cured Light Hide, 2 acid) and Helm (125, req 25, +13 Sta +12 spell: 12 Medium Leather, 2 Cured Medium Hide, 3 acid; the finished helm also drops in Blackfathom and the Stockade) - the Armor pattern is a bind-on-pickup drop from Oggleflint in Ragefire Chasm, a Horde dungeon (QuestieDB 1.0.11, 6 Nov), checked at Fimble in chapter 02; no Pants or Helm pattern exists. Brawler's Leather is the Str/Agi version: same skills and Pristine Leather, Shadowgem in place of the acid - plus [TAR256730 Stondry Darkhammer] (10.2,74.2) for Blacksmithing plans and Alchemy/Enchanting/Engineering/Tailoring/Cooking vendors, and [TAR258878 Auctioneer Quickcoin] (9.4,71.8): an auction house without the trip to Stormwind [G10.2,72.0 Redridge Mountains]
